Subject: [PATCH] serialize asynchronous HAL initialization, close and shutdown

Wait for both the initialize method reply and completion callback before closing.
Keep GLib servicing HAL callbacks during both transactions. Preserve latest power
intent, finish kernel HCI setup before close, and bound the complete shutdown.

Cancel lifecycle transactions on failure and teardown. A dead HAL invalidates the
whole vhci session: exit for the supplied service to recreate it, rather than
reattaching a new HAL to stale HCI state. Never issue synchronous CLOSE after the
main loop has stopped. This also removes the old blocking reconnect loop.

Upstream-Status: Pending

